  "instance_name": "swimming_ability_stereotype",
  "label": "Stereotype: Black people are naturally good swimmers",
  "description": "This is a harmful and racist stereotype that falsely claims Black people have an innate or superior ability to swim. It is used to demean and stereotype Black individuals, often implying they are 'natural' swimmers or that they are 'dangerous' in water due to their supposed physical traits. This stereotype is rooted in racist historical narratives and is used to justify discrimination or mockery.",
